OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F357A1786567665
OL,3,CDid a lifeguard really punch a shark
OL,4,Con a Jersey beach?
OL,6,FOn Saturday 1 August, a Jersey beach
OL,7,Fwas temporarily closed after a
OL,8,Fsuspected sighting of a shark.
OL,10,FAfter a lifeguard reported the
OL,11,Fsighting, a red flag was raised to
OL,12,Fsignal that swimmers should exit the
OL,13,Fwater.
OL,15,FOne lifeguard told media reports that
OL,16,Fhis colleague paddled near the large
OL,17,Fcreature and accidentally brushed
OL,18,Fagainst it.
OL,1,W~+$z5~{4~k4~k4~sj5  hws         G2/9
OL,2,W+.!/*%/*%/*%/*%+,"-$ /(,'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BCh Is News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,358,350,120,260,000,100
PN,35703
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F357A1786567665
OL,3,CDid a lifeguard really punch a shark
OL,4,Con a Jersey beach?
OL,6,FThe area was checked, but nothing was
OL,7,Ffound, and the coastline was reopened
OL,8,F45 minutes later.
OL,10,FWas this toothy monster the shark?
OL,12,FThis picture of a dead shark was
OL,13,Fshared widely online by social media
OL,14,Fusers who claimed it was the same
OL,15,Fshark that closed St Ouen's Bay.
OL,17,FHowever, these pictures relate to a
OL,18,Fdifferent incident in June 2026 where
OL,19,Fa 14.1-foot-long shark, weighing more
OL,20,Fthan 94 stones, washed up at Greve
OL,21,FD'Azette beach in Jersey.
OL,1,W~+$z5~{4~k4~k4~sj5  hws         G3/9
OL,2,W+.!/*%/*%/*%/*%+,"-$ /(,'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BCh Is News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,358,350,120,260,000,100
PN,35704
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F357A1786567665
OL,3,CDid a lifeguard really punch a shark
OL,4,Con a Jersey beach?
OL,6,FIt was identified as a Smalltooth sand
OL,7,Ftiger shark, which has not been found
OL,8,Fin the island since records began.
OL,9,FHowever, it has been recorded washed
OL,10,Fup on the UK shoreline.
OL,12,FIn short, there were no verified
OL,13,Fphotos of the St Ouen's Bay incident.
OL,15,FDid the lifeguard punch a shark?
OL,17,FWhile a lifeguard reported to other
OL,18,Fmedia that his colleague "kind of
OL,19,Fpunched" the shark, this was while
OL,20,Fthey were paddling nearby the large
OL,21,Fcreature.
OL,1,W~+$z5~{4~k4~k4~sj5  hws         G4/9
OL,2,W+.!/*%/*%/*%/*%+,"-$ /(,'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
