OL,24,ANext Page BCh Is News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,358,350,120,260,000,100
PN,35707
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F357A1786567665
OL,3,CDid a lifeguard really punch a shark
OL,4,Con a Jersey beach?
OL,6,FCould we see more dangerous sharks
OL,7,Fhere as the weather warms?
OL,9,FWe already get some types of "shark"
OL,10,Faround Jersey's coast - like catsharks
OL,11,For smooth hounds. These are small,
OL,12,Fharmless, and spend much of their life
OL,13,Fon the seabed.
OL,15,FExperts also believe that it is
OL,16,Funlikely that we will start seeing
OL,17,Fgreat whites or bull sharks around the
OL,18,FChannel Islands.
OL,1,W~+$z5~{4~k4~k4~sj5  hws         G7/9
OL,2,W+.!/*%/*%/*%/*%+,"-$ /(,'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BCh Is News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,358,350,120,260,000,100
PN,35708
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F357A1786567665
OL,3,CDid a lifeguard really punch a shark
OL,4,Con a Jersey beach?
OL,6,FChanges are occurring to the islands'
OL,7,Fmarine life as the seas warm due to
OL,8,Fclimate change, but experts affirm
OL,9,Fthat it is very unlikely we'll see any
OL,10,Fof these famous shark breeds anytime
OL,11,Fsoon.
OL,13,FDo I need to stay out of the sea?
OL,15,FSome headlines suggested this was the
OL,16,Ffirst time St Ouen's Bay closed, but
OL,17,Fthis is unlikely, as beaches can be
OL,18,Ftemporarily shut by lifeguards due to
OL,19,Fevents like extreme weather or strong
OL,20,Ftides.
OL,1,W~+$z5~{4~k4~k4~sj5  hws         G8/9
OL,2,W+.!/*%/*%/*%/*%+,"-$ /(,'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BCh Is News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,358,350,120,260,000,100
PN,35709
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F357A1786567665
OL,3,CDid a lifeguard really punch a shark
OL,4,Con a Jersey beach?
OL,6,FSt Ouen's Bay has also been closed
OL,7,Fseveral times over the decades for
OL,8,Fbomb disposal operations, as the beach
OL,9,Fwas heavily mined by German forces
OL,10,Fwhen the Channel Islands were occupied
OL,11,Fduring World War II.
OL,13,FAt the time of the shark sighting,
OL,14,Flifeguards thoroughly checked the
OL,15,Farea, and the coast is clear.
OL,17,FIt is advised to swim between red and
OL,18,Fyellow flags, as it is a designated
OL,19,Farea which lifeguards are observing.
OL,1,W~+$z5~{4~k4~k4~sj5  hws         G9/9
OL,2,W+.!/*%/*%/*%/*%+,"-$ /(,'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,
